From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Sosedkin <monk@unboiled.info>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:11:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Download the bootstrap zip from a URL

droid-nix installs a Nix bootstrap instead of Termux's apt bootstrap, so
nothing is embedded in the APK anymore. On first start the app asks for
the URL of the bootstrap zip, prefilled with

  https://github.com/lassulus/droid-nix/releases/latest/download/bootstrap-$ARCH.zip

and streams it from there. The dialog takes the full zip URL, so any
file name works for testing other bootstraps.

This removes the termux-bootstrap native library (ndkBuild) and the
gradle tasks that downloaded Termux's bootstrap zips at build time.

Based on nix-on-droid-app commits 2d6c9b08 ("Allow specifying a custom
bootstrap URL") by Alexander Sosedkin and fe6512ed ("build.gradle:
Remove unused bootstrap download tasks") by Zhaofeng Li.
